  "statement": "A factory must process `n` jobs in the given order. Job `i` takes `a_i` minutes. The jobs are divided into exactly `k` **consecutive** non-empty shifts. Choose the split so that the **longest shift is as short as possible**, and print the length of that longest shift.\n\n**Input.** First line `n k`. Second line the `n` durations.\n\n**Output.** One integer.\n\n**Example.**\n\nInput:\n```\n5 2\n7 2 5 10 8\n```\nOutput:\n```\n18\n```",
  "constraints": [
    "1 ≤ k ≤ n ≤ 1000 in this browser version (the idea scales to 2·10^5)",
    "1 ≤ a_i ≤ 10^9"
  ],
  "timeLimitMs": 1000,
