  "hints": [
    "Suppose someone tells you the longest shift may be at most `C`. Can you decide quickly whether `k` shifts suffice?",
    "Greedy: keep adding jobs to the current shift until the next one would exceed `C`, then start a new shift. Count the shifts.",
    "If the greedy needs at most `k` shifts, `C` is feasible (extra shifts can always be created by splitting). Binary search the smallest feasible `C` between `max(a)` and `sum(a)`."
  ],
  "editorial": "`ok(C)`: greedily fill shifts, starting a new one only when forced. The greedy uses the fewest possible shifts for the cap `C`, so `ok(C)` is true iff the minimum number of shifts is at most `k`. If fewer than `k` shifts are used we can split some shift to reach exactly `k` because `k ≤ n` and splitting never increases the maximum.\n\n`ok` is monotone in `C`, the lower bound is `max(a)` (a single job must fit) and the upper bound `sum(a)`. Binary search gives `O(n log(sum a))`; a DP over `(parts, prefix)` would be `O(k n^2)`.",
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(n log n)",
    "space": "O(1)"
  },
  "starter": {
    "python": "import sys\n\n# Minimise the largest of k consecutive segment sums.\ndata = sys.stdin.read().split()\n# your code here\n",
    "javascript": "// Minimise the largest of k consecutive segment sums.\n// readLine() returns the next line of input (or null).\n// your code here\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    // Minimise the largest of k consecutive segment sums.\n    // your code here\n}\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner in = new Scanner(System.in);\n        // Minimise the largest of k consecutive segment sums.\n        // your code here\n    }\n}\n"
  },
  "solutions": {
    "python": "import sys\n\ndef main():\n    d = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    n, k = int(d[0]), int(d[1])\n    a = list(map(int, d[2:2 + n]))\n\n    def ok(cap):                     # can we cut into at most k parts of sum <= cap?\n        parts, cur = 1, 0\n        for x in a:\n            if cur + x > cap:\n                parts += 1\n                cur = x\n            else:\n                cur += x\n        return parts <= k\n\n    lo, hi = max(a), sum(a)\n    while lo < hi:\n        mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n        if ok(mid):\n            hi = mid\n        else:\n            lo = mid + 1\n    print(lo)\n\nmain()\n",
    "javascript": "const __L = [];\nlet __s;\nwhile ((__s = readLine()) !== null) __L.push(__s);\nconst T = __L.join(' ').split(/\\s+/).filter((x) => x.length).map(Number);\nconst n = T[0], k = T[1];\nconst a = T.slice(2, 2 + n);\nfunction ok(cap) {\n  let parts = 1, cur = 0;\n  for (const x of a) {\n    if (cur + x > cap) { parts++; cur = x; } else cur += x;\n  }\n  return parts <= k;\n}\nlet lo = Math.max(...a), hi = a.reduce((s, x) => s + x, 0);\nwhile (lo < hi) {\n  const mid = Math.floor((lo + hi) / 2);\n  if (ok(mid)) hi = mid; else lo = mid + 1;\n}\nconsole.log(String(lo));\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static StreamTokenizer st;\n\n    static long nl() throws IOException {\n        st.nextToken();\n        return (long) st.nval;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        st = new StreamTokenizer(new BufferedInputStream(System.in));\n        int n = (int) nl(), k = (int) nl();\n        long[] a = new long[n];\n        long lo = 0, hi = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            a[i] = nl();\n            lo = Math.max(lo, a[i]);\n            hi += a[i];\n        }\n        while (lo < hi) {\n            long mid = (lo + hi) / 2;\n            int parts = 1;\n            long cur = 0;\n            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n                if (cur + a[i] > mid) { parts++; cur = a[i]; } else cur += a[i];\n            }\n            if (parts <= k) hi = mid; else lo = mid + 1;\n        }\n        System.out.println(lo);\n    }\n}\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    int n, k;\n    scanf(\"%d %d\", &n, &k);\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    long long lo = 0, hi = 0;\n    for (auto &v : a) {\n        scanf(\"%lld\", &v);\n        lo = max(lo, v);\n        hi += v;\n    }\n    while (lo < hi) {\n        long long mid = (lo + hi) / 2;\n        int parts = 1;\n        long long cur = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            if (cur + a[i] > mid) { parts++; cur = a[i]; } else cur += a[i];\n        }\n        if (parts <= k) hi = mid; else lo = mid + 1;\n    }\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", lo);\n}\n"
  }
